1790107488876636	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEymRA		item.comment	bn-12plt	{"body":"Committed 0f4c511 in ws bn-12plt (not merged). RFC 0026 corrected to per-artifact PublicationAborted contract (correction 48): earlier records MAY be published (complete, receipted, immutable, GC roots), root never published, record k and later not published, residue step function of phase, retry converges. Same text fixed in IDL ErrorCode doc (IDL 1.12, doc-only, protocol stays 3.6; IDL_VERSION bumped), vocabulary.rs, workspace.rs seal_fault detail, publication.rs quote, output.rs, RFC 0030. RFC 0032 promote keeps its stronger all-or-nothing rule, now marked as stronger than the floor. gate_g1_06 pin renamed a_partial_composite_publication_meets_rfc_0026s_per_artifact_contract and asserts all five clauses over all three phases. NEW FINDING, pinned as-is: a same-key retry after PublicationAborted replays the recorded abort with retryable:false (daemon/mod.rs step 7 records faults in the replay ledger; Fault::new sets retryable false). RFC 0026 says a same-key retry is a fresh publication and the code is retryable. Not fixed here. just check: pass."}	blake3:azmhsupVjevQgOwqQlkr6gQKrdxkOfpNbxbBymaydeI
1790107545383199	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEymhA		item.create	bn-1gj9z	{"description":"Found by bn-12plt while correcting RFC 0026's PublicationAborted text. A retry under the SAME idempotency key after PublicationAborted does not publish again: it returns the recorded abort with retryable:false. RFC 0026 says PublicationAborted is retryable and that a retry is a fresh publication. Cause 1: Daemon::dispatch step 7 (crates/continuumd/src/daemon/mod.rs) writes failed outcomes to the replay ledger. Cause 2: Fault::new always sets retryable:false. Pinned as-is in gate_g1_06_acceptance.rs::a_partial_composite_publication_meets_rfc_0026s_per_artifact_contract (same-key replay block). Fix direction: decide per RFC 0026 idempotency rules which outcomes enter the replay ledger (a retryable failure must not be pinned by the key), and set retryable per the error taxonomy. Daemon conformance fix, no wire shape change. Flip the pin so the same-key retry converges on the published root with no duplicate records.","kind":"task","labels":["req:g1-03"],"title":"same-key retry after PublicationAborted replays the recorded abort; RFC 0026 declares it retryable (bn-12plt)"}	blake3:qXJmz_1Mxq5h4VsiRxWqAYanZFiotQL6Z-BNNKtYGY0
