1790107971573353	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyphA		item.comment	bn-1gj9z	{"body":"Fix committed in ws. errors::retryable (exhaustive, from RFC 0026 taxonomy: StatusConflict, QuotaExhausted, PublicationAborted = true) feeds Fault::new. dispatch step 7 skips the ledger for retryable failures. g1_06 same-key pin flipped: retry converges on root, no duplicates, success then replays. Workspace tests pass. just check: all green except lead-owned PLAN_BONE_TRACEABILITY staleness; lean passes."}	blake3:RtTujZ3onAzRE0-HuKAQSgm69UZWRmYjpBVvlRFsYRM
1790107976776095	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEypxA		item.comment	bn-1z09m	{"body":"Lead blocker fixed (4d0a95d, 62a2415). RFC 0026 Task lifecycle governs: terminal status never changes; a terminal non-Completed identity answers verification.start ok on the observing lane (F20). So a Failed resolution is final: a re-issued start answers that lane and creates no live entry. A Settled resolution is superseded explicitly (TaskTable::supersede) and the campaign re-runs to Completed with the same record. Tests: a_restart_then_the_same_start_leaves_one_state_for_a_failed_resolution, a_restart_then_the_same_start_supersedes_a_settled_resolution. task_lifecycle_schedule_matrix restart sweep now asserts both arms (9 re-run, 18 Failed-final). just check: only dossier PLAN_BONE_TRACEABILITY staleness."}	blake3:SDhqyyALCYa8oLBHdDxOgf3IUEeq76gixzmickjRTN4
1790108035730644	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyqBA		item.comment	bn-27mx7	{"body":"Commit 435ee34 in ws bn-27mx7. F1/F2: every currency StaleSnapshot (fork, seal, verification.start, task.resume) carries one Error.recovery offer workspace.seal{lineage head ws_*}, rationale reseal_lineage_head, from LineageError::Stale::current() mapped via new DaemonState::workspace_at (answers only if unique). Offers travel typed beside the envelope (OperationOutcome.recovery), filtered under N2 via admission::admit in dispatch, encoded into NextOperation by the transport. Error.data stays absent (no declared shape). No IDL/protocol/schema change. F6: context.expand agreement refusal offers the caller's own request under reissue_without_snapshot_pin; the two predicates are told apart by NextOperation.rationale, no new code. workspace.diff: now checks held (else denied) and sealed (else StaleSnapshot + reseal offer, RFC 0031); currency deliberately not checked. F3: no operation needed for recovery, because a refused caller now gets the head in the refusal. Residual gap: no proactive head query, and a capability N2 denies workspace.seal gets an empty recovery and still cannot learn the head. Pins flipped to guards in gate_g2_04; g2_02 recovery pin became an executable-offer probe (wire-level). Moved: dx03 attack 6 diff code, daemon_operations diff test, dx10/pr10_c5 byte pins (+636 result B), CLI golden pr13-11. ErrorData::CertificateRejection boxed for result_large_err. just check: pass."}	blake3:BUK2yHCg-X8dBclVLbvvkKr2kVZIawEzND4CCpt5Q3E
1790108062534492	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyqRA		item.move	bn-1z09m	{"state":"done"}	blake3:fGFNhgR6XaJq_FwBJgx_Zl0dS_PvC0pQuMlClXvNF1w
1790108062827050	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyqhA		item.comment	bn-20142	{"body":"Lead: consequence of bn-1z09m (merged adc2538) until this lands: a parked campaign resolves to Failed(ContinuationNotDurable) on restart, and RFC 0026 terminal-status rule makes that identity final, so a client must restart with a different budget (new identity). The resume branch here removes that cost."}	blake3:M3sXX8sv6e98vi8H2tW0KPFrsrh9fo5g-_CCYp6lBoA
1790108127546243	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyqxA		item.comment	bn-k99dt	{"body":"Fixed: StoreAudit::fsck now takes the declared identifier as an explicit argument instead of self.store.identifier. recovery::recover (continuumd) passes Blake3Identity explicitly; every other caller (15 files) passes the identifier its fixture already builds over. Flipped both pinned acceptance tests to regression guards: gate_g1_08_acceptance.rs's negative_control_a_substituted_identity_seam_is_caught_by_the_census_and_missed_by_fsck is renamed regression_a_substituted_identity_seam_is_caught_by_fsck_against_the_declared_seam and now asserts 3 IdentityMismatch defects; gate_g1_01_acceptance.rs's negative_control_a_non_blake3_seam_is_self_consistent_and_fails_this_files_predicate keeps its name (still accurate) and now asserts fsck(&Blake3Identity) flags every substituted entry. Also fixed g1_crash_recovery_evidence.rs's DriftingIdentity mutant control, which relied on fsck re-invoking the store's own identifier a second time at audit (no longer happens): it now derives real BLAKE3 while honest and a bogus hash from its first call when corrupt. just check: pass (fmt, clippy, all workspace tests, crate boundaries, dossier validator, lean build, axiom manifest)."}	blake3:0RS2fWPEjBfPyHlIF5ccqaunOeUozfr4vJngfHRq4dI
